    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "exactly. you get it. but it was so much more complex back then—it wasn't just about ships, it was about the quiet influence behind the scenes. i remember how we had to manage the local governors' ambitions to keep the central authority's grip firm. looking at the way these modern actors are acting, it feels like they've forgotten the importance of that internal stability. do you think the current regional leaders are making the mistake of ignoring their own internal political pressures in favor of these external displays?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
